          "id": "07914e3f35ef4b33c805c5c39b86ddf512d6f4b0",
          "message": "tests: Reduce testing of arbitrary slang expressions (#12498)\n\nThe point of using Slang in lock files is to encode OPAM expressions in a\nDune form. This means that we just need to test that we can encode\nthese.\n\nThere is no need to test for a large range of invalid inputs because the\nlock files are not supposed to be written by hand. They are supposed to\nbe emitted by Dune and if Dune is emitting invalid Slang it is a problem\nof the emitting code and needs to be fixed.\n\nThis PR removes some error messages that are emitted by the Slang\ndecoder - they are not specific to Dune pkg and should be tested\nelsewhere (e.g. `run-parse-error.t` tests for unexpected lists).\n\nSigned-off-by: Marek Kubica <marek@tarides.com>",
          "timestamp": "2025-09-29T16:42:15+02:00",
          "tree_id": "da5e119d424dff279bfdaa7daf4a00ddf5c8db34",
