          "id": "d6378d8aa598f1d688e3dc707ec454b1288da8ff",
          "message": "Generate rules for dev tools without feature gate (#12575)\n\nEnabling the `lock_dev_tools` feature was originally intended to cause\ndune to lock and install dev tools when running commands other than\nthose commands under the `dune tools` group. If a user runs `dune tools\ninstall`, they are indicating their intention to lock the tool if\nnecessary, as a first step to installing the tool, regardless of whether\nthe `lock_dev_tools` feature is enabled.\n\nThis would have been caught by CI if tests of the `dune tools install`\ncommand didn't enable the `lock_dev_tools` feature. Thus this change\nalso disables that feature (the default) for these tests.\n\nFixes https://github.com/ocaml/dune/issues/12574\n\nSigned-off-by: Stephen Sherratt <stephen@sherra.tt>",
          "timestamp": "2025-10-15T12:31:19+11:00",
          "tree_id": "e244810865879f53054708fd93020423ae1649f4",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/d6378d8aa598f1d688e3dc707ec454b1288da8ff"
