          "id": "f0c50b7f05b1bee790d7a509c85017c3c2d38d36",
          "message": "Add test for duplicate pins (#13236)\n\nI noticed that there is no test that checked the `\"package %S is already\ndefined\"` message:\n\n```sh\n$ rg \"package .* is already defined\"\nsrc/dune_lang/dune_project.ml\n513:          \"package %s is already defined in %S\"\n813:      [ Pp.textf \"package %s is already defined\" (Package.name p |> Package.Name.to_string)\n\nsrc/dune_lang/pin_stanza.ml\n32:      [ Pp.textf \"package %S is already defined\" (Package_name.to_string name) ]\n\ntest/blackbox-tests/test-cases/pkg/pin-stanza/duplicate-pins.t\n46:  Error: package \"dep_a\" is already defined\n\ntest/blackbox-tests/test-cases/exclusive-package-dirs.t\n19:  Error: package foo is already defined in \"foo\"\n```\n\nSo I wrote a test. It works properly. Thus I was curious what happens if\nI declare a duplicate pin via a dependency. It gets ignored (which come\nto think of it, is probably the right thing to do). See the test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Marek Kubica <marek@tarides.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-09T10:26:52+01:00",
          "tree_id": "884a260410df174620fbdf912df3c433722f95d2",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/f0c50b7f05b1bee790d7a509c85017c3c2d38d36"
