          "message": "fix: stop defaulting to the diff fallback inside dune (#13456)\n\nThis behavior was introduced to make the tests more portable.\nUnfortunately, it creates in behavior with the actual dune that gets in\nthe way of testing some features.\n\nWe already depend on a bunch of external programs for the tests, so I'm\nnot sure why we can't depend on \"diff\" or \"git\" either.\n\nThe new default diff program when inside dune is now `diff`. As it is\ncommonly available and works uniformly across the various platforms. I\nhad to adjust some flags to make its output reproducible\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
