          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b0bfad0c91178b07834e740c17ce079f8b746089",
          "message": "Js_of_ocaml: share standalone runtimes (#13621)\n\nAt the moment, in separate compilation mode, we are building one custom\nruntime per executable, even though the same runtime could be used by\nthe different executable.\n\nThe first commit implement the sharing at the level of a stanza, while\nthe second commit extends it to workspace-wide sharing.\n\nI'm not completely sure the added complexity is worth it. A clean run of\nthe Js_of_ocaml test suite go from 3 minutes down to 2m40 with this\nchange, but it's kind of extreme.\n\n@hhugo What do you think?\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Jérôme Vouillon <jerome.vouillon@gmail.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-03-17T19:46:35Z",
          "tree_id": "0214e24317362aa228d604e254d0bc222a1f5f49",
