          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b4050f238ad32de92a2033e1ed1a2845d2ac9bb2",
          "message": "test: document module name shadowing between stanza and library (#4572) (#14031)\n\nAdd a test documenting module name shadowing behavior between a stanza's\ninternal modules and an unwrapped library dependency.\n\nWhen an executable has a module `Helper` and also depends on an\nunwrapped\nlibrary that exposes a module `Helper`, the internal module takes\nprecedence:\nthe build succeeds using the internal module, and the library's `Helper`\nis\ninaccessible (`Unbound value`).\n\nThis behavior is relevant to #4572 (finer dependency analysis between\nlibraries), where `ocamldep` output is used to determine which libraries\na\nmodule references. Since the compiler resolves shadowed names to the\ninternal\nmodule, `ocamldep` reports the internal name — filtering it out as\nstanza-internal (rather than treating it as a library reference) is\ncorrect.\n\nRef: #4572\n\nSigned-off-by: Robin Bate Boerop <me@robinbb.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-09T10:05:24+02:00",
          "tree_id": "876858e5e133bcc9515aab552334d31f8d9b8896",
