          "distinct": true,
          "id": "875d02855935532fc346a456cd5ec43f88183de7",
          "message": "fix(ci): add bash shell defaults to Windows build job to prevent error masking (#14306)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe Windows CI jobs in the `build` job use PowerShell by default for\n`run:` steps. PowerShell does **not** stop execution when an external\ncommand returns a non-zero exit code — only the **last** command's exit\ncode is propagated.\n\nThis means in multi-line `run:` blocks like:\n\n```yaml\n- run: |\n    opam pin -n . --with-version=3.23.0\n    opam install dune --deps-only\n```\n\nIf `opam pin` fails, `opam install dune --deps-only` still runs. If that\nsecond command succeeds, the step is reported as successful — masking\nthe actual failure.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `defaults: run: shell: bash` to the `build` job. This causes all\n`run:` steps to use:\n- `bash --noprofile --norc -eo pipefail` on all platforms\n- On Windows: Git Bash (available on all GitHub Actions Windows runners\nvia Git for Windows)\n- On Linux/macOS: native bash (same as the previous default)\n\nThe `-e` flag in bash causes it to exit immediately when any command\nreturns a non-zero status, so errors are properly propagated and the\nstep fails as expected.\n\nAll commands in the affected steps (`opam pin`, `opam install`, `opam\nexec -- make ...`, etc.) work correctly with bash on Windows since\nthey're found via PATH additions made by `setup-ocaml`.",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-24T00:13:27+01:00",
          "tree_id": "fd0dca6f5cb5949f263f1fb45f93e9089c3b7dee",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/875d02855935532fc346a456cd5ec43f88183de7"
