          "message": "test: observational baseline for per-module include flags (#4572) (#14375)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds\n`test/blackbox-tests/test-cases/per-module-lib-deps/per-module-include-flags.t`\n— an observational baseline recording the `-I` flags on a consumer\nmodule's compile command when its stanza declares two libraries but the\nmodule references just one. The test inspects the actual compile-rule\naction via `dune rules --format=json` plus a `jq` filter on the action's\n`run` argv.\n\nToday both libraries' objdirs appear on the consumer's `-I` path\n(cctx-wide injection). A future per-module filter (#14186) is expected\nto narrow this to only the referenced library, at which point the\nassertion flips to a single-entry array.\n\nCompanion to `add-unreferenced-sibling-lib.t`: that test records the\n*consequence* (consumer doesn't rebuild on stanza change), this one\nrecords the *cause* (the compile command's actual `-I` content).\n\nRelated: #4572, #14186\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Robin Bate Boerop <me@robinbb.com>",
