          "id": "c1cee5286e8ce4997cbd0b1f453eea778dd1c84d",
          "message": "fix: Throttle live sandboxes (#14464)\n\nSandbox creation used to be independent from action execution, so a\nbuild with many ready sandboxed rules could create far more sandboxes\nthan could actually run. That left sandbox directories live while the\ncorresponding actions waited for scheduler or lock slots.\n\nAdd a global sandbox throttle with 100 slots and acquire a slot before\ncreating a sandbox. Hold the slot until target extraction has finished\nand the sandbox has been destroyed, so queued sandboxed actions do not\npre-create unbounded sandbox directories.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-10T10:06:32+01:00",
          "tree_id": "5bfa1476e8d831b66c0e4096ed8cba355d8f4923",
