          "id": "44e625e63ce0fd51f72b14d5bf48008dd0aac9d2",
          "message": "docs(agents): bootstrap-vs-built dune and binary-source alignment (#14507)\n\nI think that something like this is required to avoid having agents\nhaving to learn and re-learn the same thing about \"which Dune is being\nbuilt\". I'm open to changes in the verbiage if you think it will improve\nthings.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds a note in AGENTS.md's Bootstrap Process section covering the\nbootstrap-vs-built dune distinction: `_boot/dune.exe` (the binary behind\n`./dune.exe`) is built once by `make bootstrap` and is not refreshed on\nsource changes. Experiments that exercise dune's rule generation should\nuse `_build/install/default/bin/dune` after `make dev`.\n- Includes a binary-source-alignment checklist for debugging\ntest-vs-manual or CI-vs-local divergence — the commonest trap is running\nexperiments with the bootstrapped `./dune.exe` while the test suite uses\nthe fully-built dune.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Robin Bate Boerop <me@robinbb.com>",
