          "id": "b8c6c7478cc0f90d06630d9a8e5d66288d66651e",
          "message": "test: pps runtime libs reach melange compile rule (#14608)\n\nPins that a `(melange.emit ...)` stanza preprocessing with a ppx whose\n`(ppx_runtime_libraries ...)` is non-empty includes globs over the\nruntime lib's `.cmi`/`.cmj` melange objdir in the compile-rule dep set —\neven though no source names the runtime lib syntactically.\n\nMelange compile rules bypass per-module narrowing today (`can_filter =\nfalse` in `module_compilation.ml`); the property holds via the wide cctx\nglob. Forward-looking guard if narrowing ever extends to melange.\n\nSigned-off-by: Robin Bate Boerop <me@robinbb.com>",
