          "id": "f15df9adbaf5f8530db03eb0f03f1ada08c985a3",
          "message": "Conservatively handle FSEvents directory invalidations (#14756)\n\nFSEvents can report directory-wide or otherwise ambiguous changes, such\nas MustScanSubDirs and directory renames/removals. A single Unknown\nevent for the directory is not enough to invalidate cached descendants,\nso report these cases as Queue_overflow and let the scheduler\nconservatively clear filesystem caches.\n\nAlso drop build-directory events before constructing Fs_memo events, and\nroute normal events through Fs_memo_event.create. Update the macOS\nfile-watcher test to reflect that build-directory events are no longer\nemitted.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-28T17:49:35+02:00",
          "tree_id": "b853698d6ff399a08eebee2280031c0ab3a277cd",
