          "id": "a7cebccbd3b5fe1fdca50cd3fbac6f3e4f3930d6",
          "message": "perf(memo): check Run.is_current before allocating fibers on the hot path (#14964)\n\nTwo behaviour-preserving fast paths on the happy path in `Exec`:\n\n- `exec_dep_node`: if the node already holds a cached value validated in\nthe\ncurrent run, add the dependency and return the value directly, instead\nof\nrouting through `consider_and_restore_from_cache_without_adding_dep` and\nthe\n  fibers it allocates.\n- `restore_from_cache`: when checking a dependency that is already\nvalidated in\n  the current run, compare timestamps directly instead of calling\n`consider_and_restore_from_cache_without_adding_dep` (which allocates a\nfiber\n  per dependency).\n\nBoth short-circuit exactly the cases the slow path returns identically.\n`dune build src/memo` and `dune runtest test/expect-tests/memo` pass\nunchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
