          "id": "931bc0b000cf0037aaf4c8de635e8085bc113992",
          "message": "perf(memo): pack a cached value's two run timestamps into one immediate (#14970)\n\nA `Cached_value.t` stores `last_changed_at` and `last_validated_at` (two\n`Run.t`s) for early cutoff. This packs them into a single immediate\n`Run.Pair.t`\n(a 31-bit delta plus a 32-bit validated timestamp), shrinking each\ncached\nvalue's record by one word — which adds up across the many cached values\na\nlarge build holds.\n\n`Run.Pair` exposes `create`/`last_changed_at`/`last_validated_at`/\n`with_last_validated_at` with the invariant `last_changed_at <=\nlast_validated_at`.\nThe existing early-cutoff tests exercise the packing.\n\n`dune build src/memo` and `dune runtest test/expect-tests/memo` pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
