          "message": "refactor(memo): build Var's cell directly instead of via a lazy knot (#14971)\n\n`Var.create` used a recursive `lazy` value so the memoized function\ncould read back\nthe variable's current value. This stores the value in a `ref` and has\nthe spec close\nover it directly, building the cell with `make_dep_node` (as `Var.Unit`\nalready does).\nThat drops the lazy self-reference.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged; the existing `Var` tests (create/read,\ninvalidation, cutoff)\ncover it. `dune build src/memo` and `dune runtest\ntest/expect-tests/memo` pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
