          "message": "feat(memo): add reset_if_necessary and track non-reproducible errors (#14990)\n\nAdds `Memo.reset_if_necessary` and tracks non-reproducible errors.\n\n`reset_if_necessary invalidation` advances the build run only when doing\nso would actually change something:\n\n- the invalidation is non-empty, **or**\n- a non-reproducible error was produced during the current run (which\nmust be retried rather than served stale from the cache).\n\nOtherwise it is a no-op, so an empty invalidation with no errors reuses\nthe cached values and does not re-run the computation.\n\nTo support the second case, Memo records the run in which it last saw a\nnon-reproducible error (`last_saw_non_reproducible_exn_at`), and `Run`\ngains a `Run.invalid` sentinel for \"never\". The existing `reset`\nbehaviour is unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
