          "id": "288f78cdf48e6fbdfa2280b160b09316929f508a",
          "message": "refactor(memo): represent cancelled computations as non-reproducible errors (#14996)\n\nDrop the `Value.Cancelled` constructor. A computation cancelled by a\ndependency cycle is now stored as a non-reproducible `Error` whose\nexception set holds the corresponding `Cycle_error.E` (with its\ndependencies cleared, as before).\n\nThis unifies cancellation with the existing non-reproducible-error\nhandling: such values are never restored from the cache and are\nrecomputed on the next run, which was already the behaviour for both\ncases separately. The cycle error now surfaces through the same path as\ncycles detected during computation, so a few cycle reports are rotated\nto a different (equally valid) starting node; the cycles, and their\ndetection, are unchanged.\n\nThis also makes `Value.t` a leaf type (`Ok | Error`) with no dependency\non the node graph, in preparation for splitting it into its own module.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
