          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7c4058cda47dde2ce01b1b717918b96c972987cd",
          "message": "dune-configurator: support `--static` in pkg-config queries (#14947)\n\nThis change makes it easier to request static-linking info from\n`pkg-config`.\n\nIt is currently possible but only through `PKG_CONFIG_ARGN` which, being\nan environment variable seems to be more intended for being set outside\nof the discover script itself. (It's strange to pass arguments locally\nby calling `Unix.setenv`.)\n\nThe second commit documents the new parameter. It also moves the\ndocumentation of `PKG_CONFIG_ARGN` to the `get` function because this is\nwhere it matters (i.e., in `let c = get … in Unix.setenv\n\"PKG_CONFIG_ARGN\" \"…\"; query c …` the env has no effect: it must be\nmoved to the `get` part).\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Raphaël Proust <code@bnwr.net>",
