          "id": "ad4f6882bc8040b0a88e0779b34569b110f4adb5",
          "message": "fix(rpc-lwt): close input when closing output (#14983)\n\nFixes #7624.\n\n`connect_chan` now uses the socket half-close primitive for the output\nchannel: closing the output channel calls `shutdown(SHUTDOWN_SEND)`\ninstead of closing the shared descriptor. This lets pending input reads\nfinish cleanly without racing on a closed fd.\n\nThe input channel owns the actual fd close. Its close hook first closes\nthe output channel, so code cannot keep writing on a descriptor that is\nabout to be closed.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
