          "message": "refactor(memo): move Cached_value, State and Table into node.ml (#15029)\n\nMove the implementations of `Cached_value`, `State`, and `Table` (and\nthe small\n`get_cached_value_in_current_run` helper) from `memo.ml` into `node.ml`,\nalongside the node-graph core types they belong with.\n\nThese were left behind in `memo.ml` when the core types moved into\n`node.ml`,\nbecause `Cached_value`'s functions (`capture_deps`, `create`,\n`confirm_old_value`) depend on `Deps`. They form a contiguous block that\nuses\nonly sibling modules (`Deps`, `Spec`, `Store`, `Run`, `Value`,\n`Metrics`) and\nthe core node types, so they relocate cleanly. `memo.ml` re-exports\n`module Table = Node.Table` for its existing consumers.\n\nPure code motion; behaviour is unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
