          "id": "7d95c06e66d2a985a4d79a112d5b35db43808378",
          "message": "refactor(memo): store the dependency graph in immutable arrays (#15064)\n\nThe series-parallel dependency graph in `Deps` keeps its `Seq` and `Par`\nsections in arrays that are built once (from a flattened list) and never\nmutated afterwards. This stores them as `Stdune.Array.Immutable.t`\ninstead of\nregular mutable arrays, so the type enforces that the dependency arrays\nshared\ninside every cached value cannot be mutated.\n\n`changed_or_not`'s parallel case hands its section array to\n`Fiber.map_reduce_array`, which operates on a regular array, so\n`Array.Immutable` gains a zero-copy `to_array_unsafe` — the inverse of\nthe\nexisting `of_array_unsafe`, safe here because `map_reduce_array` only\nreads.\n\nPure type-level change; behaviour is unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-08T18:52:49+01:00",
          "tree_id": "244593e9643a6ff412ce2532db900868f8e3cb1d",
