          "id": "d117d879c5132b71c8cf80d39ff02a3da79aee5c",
          "message": "refactor(memo): invalidate a node to Not_cached rather than Out_of_date (#15140)\n\n## What\n\n`Node.invalidate` now moves a `Cached` (or `Out_of_date`) node to\n`Not_cached` instead of `Out_of_date`.\n\nA node's `value`, `runs` and `deps` are stored flat on the node,\nindependent of its lifecycle `state`, so the cached value survives the\ntransition and is still used as the early-cutoff baseline on recompute —\n**cutoff is preserved either way.** The only observable difference is\nthat\na `Not_cached` node re-fires a `Live` event on recompute, which is the\nright signal: a node that was invalidated and is then recomputed is live\nagain in the new run.\n\nAs a bonus, `Out_of_date` is now reached only via restore (a `Cached`\nnode whose restore found a changed dependency), making that state's\nmeaning crisper.\n\nNo behavioural change to early cutoff; the full memo test suite passes\nunchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
