          "id": "5326a3cdbb2950e6e333bd7f47cfc101beb3f60b",
          "message": "test: demonstrate missing subreaper cleanup on shutdown (#15271)\n\nAdd an isolated cram test for the scheduler shutdown cleanup path. The\ntest uses the existing setsid helper and a one-shot dune build instead\nof an RPC/watch build, so it does not pass by relying on the existing\nend-of-build subreaper cleanup.\n\nWithout the scheduler fix, the escaped child remains alive after Dune\nexits and the test prints the FAILURE branch; that branch kills the\nchild before returning so the failing test does not leak a process. The\nfollowing scheduler fix makes the expected SUCCESS output true.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-21T23:23:16+01:00",
