          "message": "docs: clarify dune install --prefix directory layout (#15306)\n\nDocuments the directory-layout behavior reported in #5733.\n\n`dune install --prefix=P` derives per-section directories using the opam\nlayout — notably `man` → `<prefix>/man` and `doc` → `<prefix>/doc`\n(*not* under `<prefix>/share`) — and `--prefix` takes precedence over\ndirectories configured at build time via `./configure`. This is by\ndesign (it matches opam's own layout), but it surprises distribution\npackagers doing FHS system installs, who expect `<prefix>/share/man`\netc.\n\nThis clarifies the *Destination Directory* section of the manual: it\nlists the per-section flags, documents the opam-style `--prefix`\ndefaults, notes the `--prefix`-over-`./configure` precedence, and shows\nthe explicit `--mandir`/`--docdir` invocation that produces the FHS\nlayout. It also fixes a stale flag name (`--lib` → `--libdir`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
