          "message": "Shell command completion (#14779)\n\nFollow-up to #14636, which bumped the version of cmdliner to 2.1.1\nThis version bump allows us to use the command completion features of\ncmdliner for supported shells: `bash`, `zsh`, and `powershell`.\n\n### What is included\nFor supported shells\n- (sub)command completion: `dune b<tab> -> dune build`\n- (sub)command suggestion `dune init <tab> -> executable library ...`\n- flag completion & suggestion `dune build --pro <tab> -> --profile\n--promote-install-files`\n\n### What is NOT included\n- Target completion `dune build <tab> -> @test @install ...`. The code\ninfrastructure for this isn't present in dune yet, from what I\nunderstand it'd be a significant undertaking.\n- Completion for fish :fish: :cry: \n\n### Experimental testing\nI was only able to test that this works in bash on my machine, reviewer\nhelp for zsh and more importantly powershell would be welcome.\nTo test this PR:\n- For bash ([you might need this\nfirst](https://github.com/scop/bash-completion)), either run `dune\ncompletion bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/dune`, or\nadd `eval \"$(dune completion bash)\"` to your bashrc\n- For zsh ([you might need this\nfirst](https://github.com/zsh-users/zsh-completions)), run `dune\ncompletion zsh > ~/.local/share/zsh/site-functions/_dune`, and make sure\nthat directory is in your `$fpath`: you might need to add\n`fpath+=~/.local/share/zsh/site-functions` to your .zshrc before\n`compinit`.\n- For powershell, either run `dune completion pwsh >>\n$PROFILE.CurrentUserCurrentHost` or add `Invoke-Expression\n-Command $(dune completion pwsh | Out-String)` to your profile script\n\nYou should be able to see completions!\n\n### Thanks\nAll my thanks to `The cmdliner programmers` whose work made this\npossible. @dbuenzli & @WardBrian :heart:\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Ambre Austen Suhamy <ambre@tarides.com>",
