          "id": "a2259ba0e2457bbf7a5c2f73143a47a15a230f89",
          "message": "refactor(rpc): move Long_poll into its own module (#15369)\n\n## Summary\n\nMove the long-poll implementation into its own module\n`src/rpc/long_poll.ml`\n(+ `.mli`), instead of having it spread across `src/rpc/server.ml` as a\nnested\n`Handler.Long_poll` submodule plus loose top-level `Poller` / `Source` /\n`Poll_cancelled`.\n\nThis is a pure structural move with no behavioral change — a first step\ntoward\naligning the server-side long-poll implementation with the one used\ninternally\nat Jane Street (which keeps `Long_poll` as a dedicated module).\n\n## What moves\n\n`src/rpc/long_poll.ml` now holds the long-poll building blocks and state\nmachine:\n\n- the `Poller` and `Source` (`Svar | Computed`) modules,\n- the `Poll_cancelled` exception,\n- the poller `Map` / `Status` and the `make_on_poll` state machine.\n\n`src/rpc/server.ml` keeps the RPC wiring (`implement_poll` /\n`implement_long_poll` / `For_tests`) in the `Handler` builder, now\nreferring to\n`Long_poll.*`; `Poller` / `Source` / `Poll_cancelled` become thin\naliases/rebindings.\n\nThe public API (`Handler.implement_long_poll`, `Source`) is unchanged,\nand the\nexisting `test/expect-tests/dune_rpc/long_polling.ml` tests pass\nunchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
