          "message": "Allow omitting unit for 0 (#15498)\n\n## Description\nThis allows omitting the unit in number units if the number is zero. It\nchecks if the string is `\"0\"` and then calls `of_string` directly on the\nstring. There is an assumption that `\"0\"` represents zero. The\nimplementation already uses `Char.is_Digit` to find where the unit\nstarts, and `Char.is_digit` checks for decimals.\n\n## Related Issue and Motivation\n<!-- Why is this change required? What problem does it solve? -->\n<!-- If it closes an open issue, link to the issue here. -->\n<!-- Non-trivial contributions are expected to be preceded by an issue,\nas\n     per CONTRIBUTING.md. -->\n\nFixes #15496\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests added, if applicable.\n- [x] [Change log entry\nadded](../CONTRIBUTING.md#updating-the-changelog) for any user-facing\nchanges.\n- [ ] Documentation added for any user-facing changes.",
