          "id": "ae0030198297d685297bf93249e5b740f9aa53ec",
          "message": "fix(trace): handle macOS fd count errors safely (#15529)\n\nproc_pidinfo reports failure separately from the errno value. The ENOMEM\npath compared the byte-count return value directly with ENOMEM and\nreturned an untagged C integer without unwinding the CAMLparam frame.\n\nCheck errno only after proc_pidinfo reports failure and return the\ncapped count as a tagged OCaml integer through CAMLreturn.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-18T16:08:48+08:00",
          "tree_id": "9dbedc008f8115ce6daa1907d689723438df0781",
