          "id": "44ccd1935b0370be3a13d6ce352271692a7d2ecd",
          "message": "fix(blake3): validate feed ranges (#15533)\n\nThe BLAKE3 feed stubs currently pass positions and lengths to C without\nvalidating them against the input. Negative values become large unsigned\nvalues, while oversized ranges can read past the supplied string, bytes,\nor bigstring.\n\nThis PR adds regression coverage for all three entry points and\nvalidates ranges before calling BLAKE3. The bound check uses `size -\npos` after checking `pos <= size`, avoiding overflow in `pos + len`.\n\nTested with:\n\n```console\ndune runtest test/expect-tests/blake3\n```\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-19T09:52:04+08:00",
          "tree_id": "197559eb9bf807ff9fe5f996e2e0f4f2865a6358",
