          "id": "024bb58909f77b683b62631b515f1edccad9b6db",
          "message": "feat(trace): aggregate allocations by site and frame (#15703)\n\nExact allocation-stack rankings fragment a single hot allocation site\nacross every distinct caller. They also make it difficult to identify\nsubsystems that are responsible for allocations deeper in their call\ntrees.\n\nAdd two rankings to each sampled minor, direct-major, and promoted heap:\n\n- `by_site` combines exact stacks by their youngest allocation frame.\n- `by_frame` attributes a stack's samples to every frame it contains,\ncounting a repeated frame only once per stack.\n\nBoth views retain the allocation source, use the configured `top` limit,\nand include sample and estimated-word counts. Together with\n`total_samples`, truncated rankings also expose their displayed\ncoverage.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
