          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5ae16bee91a962bb07971f27b512561d0278b2a4",
          "message": "feat(trace): fall back to symbolized allocation frames (#15710)\n\nAllocation-site rankings currently use the youngest captured frame even\nwhen it has neither a name nor source location. This can collapse\notherwise actionable samples into a large `<unknown>` bucket.\n\nWalk each sampled stack from youngest to oldest and attribute the site\nto the nearest symbolized frame. The lookup reuses the existing frame\ncache, leaves all-unknown stacks as `<unknown>`, and preserves exact\nstacks unchanged.\n\nIn a no-op Dune self-build, this split a 67.4M-word `<unknown>` site\ninto symbolized callers, led by `Fiber__Scheduler.exec` at 32.9M words.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
