          "id": "17ccab3ce385def74b1c54a6cbcaae8985efb609",
          "message": "perf(dag): traverse cycle edges directly (#15717)\n\nThe incremental-cycle detector's backward and forward searches use a\ngeneric\ninterruptible fold. Each edge traversal allocates callback state,\naccumulator\npairs, and `Continue` wrappers.\n\nSpecialize the incoming and outgoing traversals as direct mutually\nrecursive\nfunctions. The edge order, fuel accounting, marking, parent updates, and\nearly\ncycle exits remain unchanged.\n\nAcross warmed no-op self-build targets this reduced minor allocation by\n2.07M\nto 2.90M words. Cachegrind instructions were neutral to 0.15% lower,\nnative\nwall time was neutral to 0.67% faster, and promoted allocation and live\nmemory\nremained effectively neutral.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-08T09:53:50+01:00",
          "tree_id": "15fda63351c63c770a694242b8b04c4ee881c89e",
