          "distinct": true,
          "id": "de449b30cf8b3e0e3f067733f96b58b4b9573f28",
          "message": "perf(engine): derive rule locations on demand (#15726)\n\nEach `Rule.t` currently retains both its provenance in `Rule.Info.t` and\na\n`Loc.t` derived from that provenance. The location is only needed for\nerrors,\nbut the extra field remains live for every rule throughout a build.\n\nRemove the redundant field and derive it from `Rule.Info.t` and the rule\ntarget\nroot when diagnostics need it. Locations from dune files are returned\ndirectly;\nlocations for internal and source-copy rules are reconstructed using the\nsame\nlogic previously used by `Rule.make`.\n\nA generated 20,000-rule workload improved task-clock by about 2.2% and\nwall\ntime by about 2.5%. Self-build measurements also showed approximately\n0.5--0.9%\nless live heap.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-08T23:10:41+01:00",
