          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b76d66ada099ff935d2962c55e98f803f7cb5065",
          "message": "perf(digest): buffer manual digest input (#15731)\n\n`Dune_digest.Manual` currently crosses the OCaml/C boundary for every\nencoded\ninteger, boolean, digest, and short string. Rule hashing performs many\nof these\nsmall writes.\n\nBatch small writes in a shared 4KB buffer, flushing for representation\nhashing,\nlarge strings, finalization, and nested uses of the singleton hasher.\nExisting\ndigest values and cache keys are preserved; the added expect tests cover\nbuffer\nboundaries, large strings, mixed encodings, and representation hashing.\n\nAcross 40 alternating warmed pairs, task-clock improved by about 2.3% on\n`@install` and 2.2% on `@check` after trimming outliers. This is an\ninternal\nimplementation change and does not require a changelog entry.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
