          "id": "ac91b65af5f045120a6227bdad088005213975a2",
          "message": "perf(fiber): defunctionalize scheduler computations (#15723)\n\nReplace Fiber's closure-heavy internal CPS machinery with typed\nrepresentations for computations, continuations, deferred scheduler\nwork, parallel completion, error handling, and finalization. The public\nFiber API is unchanged, and caller-provided callbacks remain opaque\nfunction payloads.\n\nThe performance commits build on the focused behavior coverage merged\nseparately as #15743. They remain ordered by representation change:\ncontinuation and unwind frames first, then computation and scheduler\nwork nodes, followed by parallel, error-handling, and finalization\nspecializations. A test immediately before the finalization change\ncovers every body/finalizer outcome combination.\n\nRelease-build measurements of the Fiber implementation before rebase\n(`86f50a95ea6a` against `4902ebee6cf5`) showed:\n\n- null `@check` wall time: -2.18%\n- null `@check` maximum RSS: -9.0%\n- full `@check` maximum RSS: -10.9%\n- minor allocation: -17.3% null and -14.6% full\n- promoted allocation: approximately -12%\n\nFull-build CPU time was effectively neutral; full-build wall time\nremained too variable to claim a change. Incrementally, direct\nfinalization reduced full `@check` minor allocation by about 0.21% and\npromoted allocation by about 0.32%; null builds were neutral.",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-09T22:12:22+01:00",
          "tree_id": "d461581bb46e68ef3a305379660a3a6431bd5e2a",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/ac91b65af5f045120a6227bdad088005213975a2"
