          "id": "96e7b27d6a632624bf2aeee27fbaa84c393a11db",
          "message": "perf(stdune): reuse rendered environment bindings (#15745)\n\n`Env.to_unix` currently rebuilds every `KEY=value` string when each\nderived environment is first rendered, even though the persistent map\nshares most unchanged bindings.\n\nStore each value with a lazily populated `Option.Unboxed` rendering\ncache. Derived environments then share rendered strings for unchanged\nbindings, while environments never converted to Unix form avoid those\nallocations entirely. Hashing uses only immutable variable/value data so\npopulating the cache cannot change `Env.hash`.\n\nGeneralize the allocation-efficient path join into\n`String.append_with_char` and use it for environment bindings and\nslash-separated paths.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-09T22:26:53+01:00",
          "tree_id": "d7b96f3b4b2b728a77c40a924e00bfc7ff312352",
