          "id": "56c179b451e25fc8055bc8fc533da447f820b3d2",
          "message": "perf(rules): reuse parsed transitive dependencies (#15963)\n\nTransitive OCaml dependency lookups cached only the serialized\nmerge-action output. Consumers needing modules could consequently repeat\nline splitting, module-name validation, map lookup, and construction of\na separate memo node.\n\nCache the serialized output together with its parsed module list in the\nexisting keyed memo. The serialized representation is abstract and can\nonly be constructed from internal module values or by the merge action,\nwhich makes skipping redundant compatibility validation safe. Memo\ncutoffs continue to compare the serialized action output, preserving\nincremental invalidation behavior.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-20T21:18:53+01:00",
          "tree_id": "de2c82d1db9acc2b176c33880e440831f7b3d02e",
