          "id": "b80827cb0f756981a7f6ee853f6224d539fed2c8",
          "message": "fix(engine): reject colons in context names (#16085)\n\nContext names become build-directory components and must remain\nportable. Reject `:` alongside `/` and `\\`, since Dune path parsing\ntreats colons as separators on Windows and Cygwin. This deliberately\nrejects existing context names containing colons rather than\ninterpreting them differently across platforms.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
