          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2150e0c6643ac224b79d27078cd5900d4d33347a",
          "message": "test(spawn): scope filesystem fixtures to each test (#16206)\n\n## Description\n\nMove the spawn cwd fixtures into a `with_sub` helper backed by\n`Temp.with_temp_dir`.\n\nEach cwd expect test creates `sub/{foo,bar}` inside its own temporary\ndirectory. `Temp.with_temp_dir` removes the fixture when the test\ncallback finishes. This eliminates both the top-level filesystem\nmutation and the manual cleanup block at the end of `tests.ml`.\n\nDune runs inline-test partitions concurrently in the same sandbox. Every\nrunner initializes each linked module before selecting its partition, so\nthe former top-level `Unix.mkdir \"sub\"` could race even when a runner\nselected `landlock_tests.ml`.\n\n## Related Issue and Motivation\n\nFixes #16203\n\n## Testing\n\n- `nix develop path:. -c _boot/dune.exe runtest\notherlibs/stdune/test/spawn --force`\n- 16 concurrent `tests.ml` inline-test runners: 16/16 exited\nsuccessfully; with the original shared fixture, 15/16 failed with\n`EEXIST`\n- `nix develop path:. -c dune fmt`\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests added, if applicable. The affected code is test setup and\nthe existing inline tests exercise it.\n- [x] [Change log entry\nadded](../CONTRIBUTING.md#updating-the-changelog) for any user-facing\nchanges. Not user-facing.\n- [x] Documentation added for any user-facing changes. Not user-facing.",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-25T23:39:39+02:00",
          "tree_id": "c9e06e5066cd82b01a46877955cfcb468d4517a2",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/2150e0c6643ac224b79d27078cd5900d4d33347a"
