          "id": "05ab9f81088c8ccbb2b861991c8a6a71692b7990",
          "message": "fix(memo): preserve table nodes across global invalidation (#16075)\n\nFollow up on #16068 by removing the table eviction that originally made\nglobal Memo invalidation unsafe. Eviction breaks the canonical\ninput-to-node mapping: lazy nodes can retain and recompute an evicted\nnode, while later table lookups create and invalidate a disconnected\nreplacement.\n\nKeep table entries in place and invalidate their nodes instead. This\npreserves node identity while still forcing every cached computation to\nrecompute. Rename the operation from `clear_caches` to\n`invalidate_caches` to reflect its semantics.\n\nRelated to #16052.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
