          "message": "test(package-deps): retain stubs without uninstalled objects (#16348)\n\nAdds an independent installed-library fixture for foreign artifacts in\npackage dependencies. Related to #15511.\n\nLibrary `a` requires `b`, whose OCaml code actually calls a C primitive.\nThe test verifies that the installed stub archive and DLL exist, while\nthe intermediate object named by `dune-package` does not.\nCompiler-specific object, archive, and DLL suffixes are used throughout.\n\nThe consumer must build and run successfully despite that absent\nintermediate. Both metadata readers retain compile/run coverage.\nLabelled dependency observations snapshot the currently untracked\nrequired library and stubs, alongside the excluded intermediate, so\nignoring the entire support library cannot satisfy the fixed\nexpectations.\n\nThis test-only PR preserves successful behavior while recording the\nmissing dependency tracking. It passes before the implementation fix.\nApplying the follow-up fix was verified to make the required\ndependencies tracked without requiring the absent object.\n\nIncludes the five-line file-or-selector query helper also used by\n#16345. It contains no other provider test changes or implementation\nfixes, and needs no user-facing documentation or changelog entry.\n\nValidation: `@check @fmt` and `installed-foreign-object.t` passed\nindependently on this pre-fix change.",
