          "id": "ec8146cfcaa42f26099e918b8efe9e47e6d861c8",
          "message": "ci: avoid opam Git maintenance race (#16353)\n\n## Description\n\nForce Git's automatic GC and maintenance to remain in the foreground in\nevery workflow that uses `ocaml/setup-ocaml`.\n\nThis prevents opam 2.5 from recursively copying its repository while a\ndetached Git maintenance process creates and removes\n`.git/objects/maintenance.lock`.\n\n## Motivation\n\nUbuntu opam setup jobs have been failing intermittently with:\n\n```\n\"lstat\" failed on ~/.opam/repo/default/.git/objects/maintenance.lock:\nNo such file or directory\n```\n\nThis is the race reported in\n[ocaml/opam#7031](https://github.com/ocaml/opam/issues/7031). The\nupstream mitigation in\n[ocaml/opam#7073](https://github.com/ocaml/opam/pull/7073) is currently\nonly available in opam 2.6 prereleases, while `setup-ocaml` selects\nstable opam 2.5.2.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `./dune.exe build @check @fmt`\n- `./dune.exe runtest .github/workflows`",
