          "id": "8e0cc96b0adede9b55021ed17ca8a76924b324e2",
          "message": "Improve `dune_pkg_lock_normalized` (#13034)\n\n1. The `sed` command didn't do the right thing, so it was replaced by\n`dune_cmd subst`\n2. `dune_cmd subst` added training newlines everywhere, but this is only\ncorrect for stdout. It shouldn't append them to files. That made files\nhave trailing newlines. This change fixes inplace editing.\n3. `dune_pkg_lock_normalized` created a file `solve-stderr.txt` in the\nfolder. Use a temporary file instead.\n\nSigned-off-by: Marek Kubica <marek@tarides.com>",
          "timestamp": "2025-12-22T16:45:39+01:00",
          "tree_id": "e37f0ba03b9180acd7484f09bb02eed2736026a8",
