          "id": "29e79e0e00ac403f2d1c58bc863b4a1f74529443",
          "message": "cram: use bash for tests (#13137)\n\nWe already rely on a bunch of gnu things, and bash is the de-facto\nstandard on linux anyway. Explicitly asking for bash does not make any\nof our code less portable, but does allow us to use more features.\n\nSome changes that were required:\n\n* Fix out right broken tests\n* Since pipefail is enabled, we emit more non-zero exit codes when\nintermediate commands\n* Some tests had to written in a less racy way because of the above\n* Use an explicit default value for variables that might be undefined\n* Always pass arguments to functions which require them\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-02T21:46:33Z",
          "tree_id": "da666c507052257ac424648e97b971d414b00667",
