          "id": "27e579541442f40a13efd97ca044512f80eae3e7",
          "message": "fix(signal-watcher): don't `assert false` on `SIGKILL` (#13370)\n\non macOS, in a subset of cases, the signal watcher will catch both\n`SIGKILL` and `SIGINT`.\n\nwe ignore `SIGKILL` instead of running `assert false`, which will kill\nthe program less spectacularly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Antonio Nuno Monteiro <anmonteiro@gmail.com>",
