          "id": "434ddbc19cd27ac63dfe5b763f62fae537ead26a",
          "message": "Stop silently hanging when build dir is locked but RPC server is not started (#13767)\n\nFixes #12685\n\nThe `wait` argument was added (or set to true initially) to prevent the\nfollowing scenario: you start an RPC server and a client (`dune build`\nfor example) at the same time, and the server doesn't have time to set\nitself up before the client tries to connect to it, and fails.\nThe opposite scenario is what is happening right now: if the client\ntries to connect to a non-existent server, it will silently wait\nforever. This is no big deal when a server is indeed on its way, but if\nit is never coming for any reason (build cancelled, process killed...),\nthe client will hang.\n\nThis PR simply flips the `wait` flag to `false` to prevent that\nbehaviour. This is a temporary fix that does not address all problems\nwith the RPC system",
          "timestamp": "2026-03-11T09:47:18+01:00",
          "tree_id": "5dc7165f0fe55c613bf3f749411d5e67d04ae353",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/434ddbc19cd27ac63dfe5b763f62fae537ead26a"
