          "id": "1c809f7f55cc3f0d4dee6293070e4f1bf0eb20a2",
          "message": "rpc: unlink unix sockets when stopping unserved server (#14565)\n\nServer.create binds Unix-domain socket paths before the server is\nserved. If the server is stopped while it is still in the initial state,\nclosing the fds is not enough: the socket path remains in the filesystem\nand the same address cannot be reused.\n\nUnlink Unix socket paths when stopping initial server sockets, and use\nthe same helper when stopping running transports.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-16T22:35:30+01:00",
          "tree_id": "65fd0fc289471a1217ca632c08e6ccc53fc42b2a",
