          "id": "7a369c2fa5b621b15535c0bb4a31aaa292202d3a",
          "message": "rpc: set SO_NOSIGPIPE on client sockets (#14593)\n\nServer-accepted sessions already disable SIGPIPE on macOS before writes\ncan happen. Sessions created by Client.connect use a client-created\nsocket, so they need the same setup before the fd is handed to Session.\n\nThis keeps client-side RPC writes consistent with server-side session\nwrites on macOS.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-18T10:34:50+02:00",
          "tree_id": "1105156f72e9e27784ceb936b21e1007f4418dac",
