          "id": "aa933ee95b613b29252a711a7e2e332d05d48eef",
          "message": "Fix FSEvents CoreFoundation path arrays (#14726)\n\nBuild the CoreFoundation array of watched paths with CFArrayAppendValue\ninstead of setting indexes in an initially empty array. The old code\nrelied on invalid indexed insertion and could crash when creating\nstreams, especially with multiple watched paths.\n\nRelease each temporary CFString after appending it to avoid leaking\nCoreFoundation references, and add a macOS regression test for watching\nmultiple paths in one stream.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-25T22:09:02+02:00",
          "tree_id": "53a14e4d2d822f2786987209965aabc20763e3cd",
