          "id": "6007cb82cbd09a3b31e061ef3854ccc602f33b4d",
          "message": "perf(memo): use a single-lookup find_or_add in custom memo stores (#15081)\n\n`Memo.create_with_store` adapts a user-supplied store module to the\ninternal\nstore instance. That adapter previously synthesised `find_or_add` as a\n`find`\nfollowed by a `set` — two hash-table lookups — because the store backend\nmodule\ntype `Store_intf.S` only required `find`/`set`.\n\nThis requires `find_or_add` directly from `Store_intf.S` (a single\nlookup) and\nhas the adapter delegate to it. The store modules actually passed\n(`Hashtbl`-based,\ne.g. `Path.Table`) already provide it, so there are no call-site\nchanges.\n\nBehaviour-preserving.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T14:51:45+01:00",
          "tree_id": "36738825e59c1103f103b8f4ae0dc74d8472239b",
