          "id": "2851a23e3ad3592a19892eb5e8a8540c319d2481",
          "message": "fix: expand path pforms to start with ./ when in same directory (#15156)\n\n`Value.string_of_path` now uses `Path.reach_for_running` instead of\n`Path.reach`. The user-visible effect is that pforms producing path\nvalues (`%{bin:...}`, `%{dep:...}`, `%{path:...}`, and friends) render\nbare-basename paths with a leading `./`. This stops shells like `bash`\nin `(bash ...)` and `(system ...)` actions from treating a\nsame-directory binary as a `PATH` lookup.\n\n`Path.reach_for_running` itself is tightened so that the current\ndirectory stays as `.` rather than becoming `./.`. Bare basenames\n(the actual hazard) still get the `./` prefix.\n\nAlso rewrites the `bin:<program>` paragraph in\n`doc/concepts/variables.rst` into three short paragraphs covering\nresolution, the `(deps ...)` PATH-symlink mechanism, and the fact that\n`(run %{bin:foo} ...)` and `(run foo ...)` behave the same.\n\n- fixes #15147",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-17T17:31:17+01:00",
          "tree_id": "9e309e01a4f8db4c0619f3ae0b74b2013e88ce36",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/2851a23e3ad3592a19892eb5e8a8540c319d2481"
