          "id": "ca40ca401a045e6ebaa01a312a03fb62f64ca316",
          "message": "stdune: tolerate disappearing proc task children files (#15277)\n\nReading Linux direct children from /proc first lists /proc/<pid>/task\nand then opens each task children file. A thread can exit between those\noperations, so ENOENT for the children file is expected and should be\nignored instead of leaking a raw path error.\n\nUse Unix.openfile for that read so ENOENT is reported as a structured\nUnix error and handled by the existing race-tolerant case.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-22T00:16:06+01:00",
          "tree_id": "b2f8e9ee35aa2b11cccad885909e7a6397b796a8",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/ca40ca401a045e6ebaa01a312a03fb62f64ca316"
