          "id": "8bd8c8f2e12a852d33eddf3bb69098cc99b82a59",
          "message": "test(promote): demonstrate #785 (--auto-promote exits non-zero) (#15283)\n\nRepro for #785.\n\nThis adds a cram test that documents the current behaviour: `dune build\n--auto-promote` applies the promotion but still exits with code `1`,\nwhich\nforces callers to wrap the command in `|| true`.\n\nThe test records the status quo (note the trailing `[1]` after\n`Promoting\n_build/default/x.gen to x.`). The follow-up fix PR will flip that `[1]`\ninto a\nsuccessful exit, demonstrating the change as a test-output diff. It also\npins\ndown two behaviours the fix must preserve:\n\n- re-running `--auto-promote` reaches a fixpoint and is a clean no-op;\n- a non-promotable diff (between two generated build artifacts) is a\ngenuine\n  failure that must keep exiting non-zero.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
