          "id": "630c7b6ef1bb9adc6323610f5ea5481f7f56d602",
          "message": "fix(lev): preserve libev system errors (#15278)\n\nKeep errno, and on Windows the Winsock last-error value, intact across\nlibev callbacks that release and reacquire the OCaml runtime lock. Libev\ninspects these values after the callbacks return, so clobbering them can\nhide the real failure or change libev error handling.\n\nAlso install a Windows syserr callback so fatal libev errors include the\nnumeric Winsock error and system message instead of just a CRT strerror\nstring.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-22T22:03:16+01:00",
          "tree_id": "9bac4ad01b97748881eee8e825478dc716476670",
