          "id": "cc57f6d61771177b0de00ad434c6a64202295c79",
          "message": "test(install): refresh stale comments in install-with-var (#15295)\n\nThe narration in `install-with-var.t` still described variable-expansion\nrestrictions on the install stanza (e.g. *\"Some variables are restricted\nin\n`[dst]` of `[bin]` section because evaluating them could cause a\ndependency\ncycle\"*).\n\nThose restrictions were removed in #10160, which dropped the\ncorresponding\nerror outputs from the test but left the explanatory comments behind, so\nthe\ncomments now contradict the (passing) commands.\n\nThis refreshes the comments to describe the current behaviour: variables\ncan be\nexpanded in the `[src]`/`[dst]` of installed files, including in the\n`[bin]`\nsection. No commands or expected outputs change.\n\nContext: #6818 asked to lift this very limitation; it was already\nresolved by\n#10160 in 3.15.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
