          "id": "df353d036da2ff6aa1f24a2e777626c0702974a9",
          "message": "refactor(nix): replace oxcaml-trunk-build with ox-minimal-trunk shell (#15311)\n\n`packages.oxcaml-trunk-build` was a bespoke `stdenv.mkDerivation` that\nhand-wired the OxCaml build inputs (dune, autoconf, menhir, findlib,\nocaml) and re-ran configure+make. Its sole consumer is\n`.github/workflows/revdeps-dev-build.yml`, which checks that OxCaml main\nstill builds.\n\nReplace it with `devShells.ox-minimal-trunk`: like `ox-minimal` but with\n`oxcaml-setup.compiler.overrideAttrs { src = fetchGit main; }`. Reuses\nthe upstream OxCaml derivation, so menhir-20231231 and the rest of the\nbuild inputs come along for free.\n\n`includeTestDeps = false` (inherited from `ox-minimal`) keeps the\nclosure narrow — entering the shell mostly only forces the trunk\ncompiler to build, which is the smoke test we want.\n\nWorkflow command becomes:\n  nix develop .#ox-minimal-trunk --impure -c true\n\nWith both the trunk-build derivation and `ox-trunk` shell gone, nothing\nconsumes `nix/menhir.nix` or `oxcaml-setup.menhir-src` anymore; delete\nboth.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-24T21:55:51+01:00",
          "tree_id": "998ff8031b95dab5b5addd34df808a7d56f584d2",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/df353d036da2ff6aa1f24a2e777626c0702974a9"
