          "id": "262a98e0422968529658164057b077079ee639a7",
          "message": "rpc server: cancel in-flight long-poll requests (#15362)\n\nWhen a client cancels a long-poll request while the server is waiting\nfor the next value, fire a per-poller cancellation token and wake the\nsource so the request fiber can stop promptly.\n\nTreat the internal Poll_cancelled exception as a completed request with\nno server response. Keep long-poll bookkeeping limited to idle/waiting\nstate, with cancellation represented only by the poller's cancel token\nand cancellation removing the poller from the map.\n\nUpdate the long-poll expect tests to cover cancelling an in-flight poll\nand continuing to use the same RPC connection afterwards.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-28T12:53:01+01:00",
          "tree_id": "1155e07d91c7ad101d4740d8b4af43c8f83c4e74",
