          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6b8651b25f851d129ff6df020c2cbe56c081d762",
          "message": "perf(engine): track pending targets in hash tables (#15672)\n\nTracking targets of running unsandboxed actions previously converted\nvalidated\ntargets and rebuilt sorted arrays whenever an action started or\nfinished.\n\nUse separate mutable path tables for file and directory targets, iterate\nvalidated targets directly, and add key-aware hash-table iteration for\ncleanup.\nThe cleanup tables are cleared even if removing a pending target raises.\n\nIn a cold Dune self-build allocation profile, the pending-target stacks\naccounted for at least 6.8M minor words and 1.33M major words (about 62\nMiB).\nThose stacks disappeared after this change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-04T08:04:43+01:00",
          "tree_id": "1c13150002d489b9b8ee30f416063c2ee2eec65e",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/6b8651b25f851d129ff6df020c2cbe56c081d762"
