          "distinct": true,
          "id": "acc48cf57f837d9accb7c92213e8f4cdc38e1bd5",
          "message": "test(watching): avoid SIGPIPE in status line test (#15692)\n\nCram tests run with `pipefail`, and `grep -m 1` or `grep -q` could exit\nwhile `tr` was still writing. Depending on output size and scheduling,\n`tr` then exited with SIGPIPE (141), making `rpc-build-status-line.t`\nflaky.\n\nLet the affected `grep` processes consume their entire streams and\nselect the first output afterward. This preserves the assertions while\navoiding SIGPIPE.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-05T09:22:20+01:00",
          "tree_id": "68c6c427f72bd460a403505484a23334c2680b55",
