          "distinct": true,
          "id": "40ff15f3eb4ed23b966ab7acb01d72f2bdd92a29",
          "message": "perf(fiber): reuse variable maps for unchanged values (#15690)\n\nAbout 13% of fiber-variable writes in a self-build store the same\nphysical value already present. Return the existing map in that case,\navoiding an array copy while preserving the dynamic-scope context.\n\nThis saved about 0.23M words (1.8 MiB) in a cold self-build and 0.90M\nwords (6.9 MiB) in a no-op build.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
