          "id": "28682b6a65d50915e811bee3ee786324ce8cf14e",
          "message": "feat(trace): configure allocation sampling from the environment (#15699)\n\nDune's allocation profiler currently hard-codes its sampling rate,\ncaptured stack depth, and number of retained top stacks. That makes it\ndifficult to trade profiling overhead for resolution and to reproduce\nhow an allocation summary was collected.\n\nAdd the experimental `DUNE_TRACE_ALLOC` setting with `rate`, `stack`,\nand `top` fields, for example:\n\n```sh\nDUNE_TRACE=+alloc DUNE_TRACE_ALLOC=rate=0.001,stack=20,top=100 dune build\n```\n\nAllocation summary events include the effective configuration, so\nreports remain interpretable after the trace is captured. Invalid\nsettings are rejected when allocation tracing starts. The existing\nhard-coded values remain the defaults.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-07T09:36:58+01:00",
          "tree_id": "1ed97c0232ff65c6b6d779b468de19257b5d8e12",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/28682b6a65d50915e811bee3ee786324ce8cf14e"
