          "id": "5b109c3cb8bf4492415168f7597405aa13bfb569",
          "message": "perf(digest): reuse representation digest state (#15707)\n\nRepresentation digest traversal currently allocates a recursive closure\nenvironment and an 8-byte scratch buffer for every top-level value. Move\nthe\ntraversal to direct mutually recursive functions so that\n`Digest.Manual.repr`\ncan reuse the manual digester's existing scratch buffer.\n\nAcross warmed no-op self-builds, this reduced minor allocation by 0.32M\nto\n0.52M words. Promoted allocation, live memory, Cachegrind instructions,\nand\nnative wall time remained effectively neutral. Digest encoding and the\npublic\nAPI are unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-08T00:23:12+01:00",
          "tree_id": "e6118b4d27df07cbc87ad493e9167854e6eadd32",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/5b109c3cb8bf4492415168f7597405aa13bfb569"
