          "id": "2ea4fe371f94e3aadef23fe31af8492e4cde76b4",
          "message": "perf(trace): sort allocation rankings once (#15728)\n\nAllocation-profile rankings currently insert every candidate into a\nbounded immutable list and immediately truncate it. With `top=100`,\nrebuilding those lists dominates snapshot allocation.\n\nSort each aggregated table once and take the requested prefix instead.\nAdd a trace assertion that exact-stack, allocation-site, and\ninclusive-frame rankings remain ordered by descending sample count.\n\nIn controlled cold `@check` profiles with `top=100`, exit-summary\nallocation fell from 54.5M to 12.8M words, while process-wide fresh\nallocation fell from 508.5M to 455.4M words.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
