          "id": "2a50b3ed77bd669df847e2059304f2198b6600b2",
          "message": "refactor(rules): thread library closure state directly (#15714)\n\nLibrary closure traversal currently layers a generic `State` monad over\n`Resolve.Memo`. Each visit therefore allocates additional closures and\nintermediate state/result pairs, while obscuring the state flow through\nthe traversal.\n\nThread the immutable closure state directly through `Resolve.Memo`\noperations instead. This keeps error accumulation and traversal order\nunchanged while removing the extra monad layer and making the state\ntransitions explicit.\n\nOn real no-op `@install` and `@check` self-builds, minor allocation fell\nby 4.6% and 4.9%, while promoted allocation remained neutral. Native\nruntime moved in the expected direction but remained within measurement\nnoise.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-09T09:39:42+01:00",
