          "id": "2d3012e9a112fc2a51a23f683b3cea55a377eae7",
          "message": "perf(digest): use primitive integer encoding (#15727)\n\nDune encodes ordinary OCaml integers as signed little-endian 64-bit\nvalues\nwhen hashing rules, actions, dependencies, and representations. Both\ndigest\npaths currently encode these values one byte at a time with `Int64`\noperations.\n\nUse `Bytes.set_int64_le` for both ordinary integers and genuine `int64`\nvalues.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-09T13:46:45+01:00",
          "tree_id": "48d214f01a959a657f128a87ad9e29502fa3b8e0",
