          "id": "1ad3797d1ba793f7ed4f5cfd9530fa6c90ea43ae",
          "message": "perf(path): append known filenames without normalization (#16099)\n\nUse `relative_fname` when appending values already known to be valid\n`Filename.t` path components, avoiding redundant conversion and\nnormalization across directory traversal, cache, package, and rule\npaths. Append external filename components directly and cover root and\ntrailing-separator behavior.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
