          "id": "8faa3d88f88feb9118d39189df964032a2cfb6d6",
          "message": "perf(sexp): fuse common decoder combinators (#16109)\n\nThe S-expression decoder interprets parser combinators through a GADT,\nso common `Bind`, `Map`, `Seq`, `And`, and `Repeat` compositions create\nintermediate value/state results and repeatedly dispatch through the\ninterpreter.\n\nHandle the common shapes generated by record decoders directly, allowing\nadjacent operations to share state. Repeated `Next` and `Enter` parsers\nalso map directly over their input, with a tail-recursive path retained\nfor long lists. General parser shapes continue to use the existing\nfallback cases.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rudi Grinberg <me@rgrinberg.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-23T09:39:33+01:00",
          "tree_id": "cc1ddb7f31dc7dd679b5218ffebd68be47724475",
