          "id": "5d83bf08d2582cbab07fb0fec0ccd264b8cf75a8",
          "message": "test(package-deps): preserve usable installed library roots (#16347)\n\nAdds an independent fixture for an installed package advertising both\nusable and unusable library roots. Related to #15511.\n\nThe usable root has library requirements `a -> b`; its sibling has\n`a.optional -> unavailable`. The test proves that the optional root is\nadvertised and initially usable, removes its requirement, then checks\nthe specific missing-dependency diagnostic with separate Dune resolver\nprobes under both metadata readers.\n\nConsumers depending on package `a` must still build and run. Keeping the\n`a -> b` requirement and labelled dependency observations ensures that\ndiscarding the entire support closure cannot masquerade as correctly\nskipping the unusable root.\n\nThis test-only PR preserves the successful consumers and intentionally\nsnapshots missing `b` dependency tracking, so it passes before the\nimplementation fix. Applying the follow-up fix was verified to change\nonly the required dependency observations; the bad-root diagnostics and\nsuccessful consumer results remain unchanged.\n\nIncludes the five-line file-or-selector query helper also used by\n#16345. It contains no other provider test changes or implementation\nfixes, and needs no user-facing documentation or changelog entry.\n\nValidation: `@check @fmt` and `installed-unavailable-sublibrary.t`\npassed independently on this pre-fix change.",
