          "id": "a5b3792564f3c27a5e09e28fc9c3f86e1438bc74",
          "message": "fix(stdune): hash Windows file descriptors by value (#16476)\n\nWindows \"file descriptors\" are OCaml heap managed wrappers around their\nunderlying handles. Naively hashing file descriptors using their\nunderlying integer values, which works on unix, breaks on Windows.\n\nThis breakage was observed in https://github.com/ocaml/dune/issues/16459\ntogether with a reproduction case submitted in\nhttps://github.com/ocaml/dune/pull/16461.\n\nWe fix this issue by resorting to `Poly.hash` on Windows.\n\n- Fixes #16459 \n- [x] changelog",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-25T13:20:25+02:00",
          "tree_id": "13fac92f96f47d623f688855656aef48929a966a",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/a5b3792564f3c27a5e09e28fc9c3f86e1438bc74"
