          "id": "82d4ebde6499bf211ba20e9b09c82d46eeeaaf4f",
          "message": "Fix builds failing with `Unbound module Stdlib` when a project uses menhir with package management (#16374)\n\n## Description\n\nThe relocatable ocaml compiler relies on platform-specific heuristics to\nfind the compiler executable, which it then uses to locate the Stdlib.\nWhen the relocatable ocaml compiler is managed as a regular package by\ndune package management, we had been (unintentionally) relying on\nbehavior that is only guaranteed on Linux to make up for a rule that did\nnot specify its dependency on the Stdlib. This allowed\nhttps://github.com/ocaml/dune/issues/15642 to surface on macOS.\n\nTo fix this error across all platforms, two fixes are required:\n\n1. The stdlib must be added as an explicit dependency for the rule that\ngenerates interfaces.\n2. In case the the path to the stdlib is located inside the `_build`\ndirectory (as it is when using dune package management with the\nrelocatable compiler), we need to reclassify the path as `Local`, to\nensure the stdlib will get linked into the sandbox where it is needed.\n\n## Related Issue and Motivation\n\nFixes #15642\n\nBuilds on and supersedes https://github.com/ocaml/dune/pull/15679",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-25T12:53:43-04:00",
          "tree_id": "f88bfa9fa14256d5e62f9ac5ff1bf137e6e27f30",
          "url": "https://github.com/ocaml/dune/commit/82d4ebde6499bf211ba20e9b09c82d46eeeaaf4f"
